  "term": "table-tilting",
  "definition": "In this historical psychology source, table-tilting refers to using a tilting table as a way to register an alleged telepathic effect. The movement of the table was taken as a sign that the impression showed itself in action before reaching the percipient’s ordinary conscious awareness.",
